---
description: CUDA/PyTorch timing and GPU inference conventions
globs:
  - "src/inference_sandbox/**/*.py"
  - "tests/system/**/*.py"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Assert `torch.cuda.is_available()` in GPU entry points and log `torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)`.
- Use `torch.cuda.synchronize()` before and after timed GPU regions.
- Prefer `torch.cuda.Event` for kernel-level timing; `time.perf_counter()` is okay for end-to-end request timing.
- Report p50/p95/p99 latency, not only mean.
- Track TTFT and TPOT separately for LLM serving benchmarks.
- Avoid hidden CPU fallback. Check model/device placement explicitly.
- Mark tests that require a real GPU with `@pytest.mark.gpu`.